{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "milestone": "M60",
  "rule": "Objective-C analyzer scaling: per-shape exponent, and real-corpus cost per KB",
  "generatedAt": "2026-09-30T03:54:46.537Z",
  "method": "each shape swept INDEPENDENTLY (methods, properties, distinct selectors, one receiver with many sends, enum members, imports) because a single size sweep varies size and symbol density together and cannot attribute a slope to either. Each shape in two variants — regular identifiers, and randomised identifiers with the same structure — because generated input is regular and a resolver that is accidentally linear on repeated structure would look quadratic here. Wall time is parse+analyze with one warm-up parse excluded; the exponent is fitted on log-log time and the per-doubling ratio is reported beside it because the ratio is what a reader can check by hand.",
  "why": "the shared O(n^2) this repo already fixed was found on YAML and was SHARED, so it is not what this probe is looking for. It is looking for three Objective-C-specific shapes nothing has ever timed: symbol density (the highest in the corpus per byte), selector cost (a selector is not a name, and edges dedup on type|source→target), and per-file cost carrying cross-file state.",
  "estimator": "minimum of N reps (N=7 for n<=1000, 5 above), with the mean and the min/mean spread recorded per point so a noisy measurement is visible rather than hidden",
